using System;

namespace AiDotNet.Attributes;

/// <summary>
/// Marks an options size that test-scale construction must leave at its value, because the number is fixed by data the
/// model reads rather than chosen for capacity: a tokenizer's vocabulary, a phoneme inventory.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <para>
/// ModelTestScale (generated by TestScaleOptionsGenerator) shrinks every integer size above its floor so a sweep can build
/// every model cheaply. A size that indexes external data cannot shrink: Grounding DINO embeds BERT-base-uncased token
/// ids, so a vocabulary under 30522 cannot hold them, and the model rightly rejects it. The attribute keeps such a size
/// out of the scaling table; it has no effect on a model a user constructs.
/// </para>
/// <para>On a property it exempts that property. On an options class it names an inherited property to exempt for that
/// class only (a VocabSize declared on a shared base whose other models do scale it).</para>
/// <para><b>For Beginners:</b> Tests build tiny versions of every model by shrinking their sizes. This tag says "this
/// number must stay as it is", because it has to match a real dictionary the model uses.</para>
/// </remarks>
[AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Property | AttributeTargets.Class, AllowMultiple = true, Inherited = true)]
public sealed class NotScaledAttribute : Attribute
{
    /// <summary>Creates the declaration.</summary>
    /// <param name="reason">What fixes the value (the data it indexes), so the exemption can be re-checked.</param>
    /// <exception cref="ArgumentException">The reason is null, empty, or whitespace.</exception>
    public NotScaledAttribute(string reason)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(reason))
            throw new ArgumentException("A size exempt from test scaling must say what fixes its value.", nameof(reason));
        Reason = reason;
    }

    /// <summary>Exempts the named (usually inherited) property of the options class carrying the attribute.</summary>
    /// <param name="propertyName">The property to leave unscaled.</param>
    /// <param name="reason">What fixes the value.</param>
    public NotScaledAttribute(string propertyName, string reason) : this(reason)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(propertyName))
            throw new ArgumentException("Name the property to leave unscaled.", nameof(propertyName));
        PropertyName = propertyName;
    }

    /// <summary>The exempt property's name when the attribute is on a class; null on a property.</summary>
    public string? PropertyName { get; }

    /// <summary>What fixes the value.</summary>
    public string Reason { get; }
}
